q(1,'Differentiate foreign investment and aid by their purpose and terms.','Investment places resources with an investment interest or return; aid assists development or humanitarian needs through differing instruments. Assistance is not automatically a non-repayable gift.',['Comparison: investment interest versus assistance purpose, with terms recognised.'])
q(2,'Suggest an appropriate assistance form for an invented clinic with trained staff and medicines but no reliable safe-water connection. Qualified technical design and connection funds are missing.','Seek suitable technical assistance and project finance or a grant for a workable maintained connection. This addresses the identified infrastructure gap rather than adding staff already available.',['Context: available clinical inputs and missing connection support.','Reason: assistance matched to the gap.'])
for n,s in [(3,'01-01'),(4,'01-02')]:q(n,'Define '+dict((x[0],x[1]) for x in E)[s].lower()+'.',L[s][0],['Meaning: '+L[s][0]])
q(5,'Explain which fictional offer better fits a low-income community’s reliable-water aim: A provides a funded maintained connection as a grant; B provides a larger loan for equipment without an operator or repayment-income plan.','A is better supported because it delivers the relevant service without the stated operating and repayment gaps. B offers more finance but may add debt without usable output; size of funding alone is insufficient.',['Judgement: compare against reliable usable water.','Reason: weigh delivery/support and repayment obligations.'])
q(6,'Explain the economic mechanism when a fictional foreign loan finances equipment that cannot operate because power and training are absent, while repayments begin immediately.','The asset supplies no expected productive benefit while debt service consumes resources. Missing complementary inputs prevent the hoped-for return, so borrowed finance alone does not establish a development gain.',['Mechanism: unusable asset plus immediate obligations.','Consequence: resource pressure without expected productive capacity.'])
q(17,'Explain why a loan and debt are not identical concepts.','A loan is the borrowing arrangement; debt is the amount still owed. Test whether the statement describes the transaction or its outstanding obligation.',['Error: transaction merged with remaining liability.','Distinction: borrowing arrangement versus amount owed.'])
q(18,'Explain why emergency relief and multilateral aid are not competing labels for the same dimension.','Emergency describes the assistance purpose; multilateral describes delivery through an international institution. An emergency programme can be multilateral; test purpose separately from delivery arrangement.',['Error: purpose and channel treated as alternatives.','Distinction: need addressed versus institutional route.'])
q(7,'Describe two considerations for assessing foreign direct investment.','It may supply productive finance or technology, but local jobs, skills and supply links determine retained gains. Ownership terms and environmental effects can limit benefits.',['Feature: a possible contribution and a relevant condition or limitation.'])
q(8,'Identify the obligation distinguishing a loan from a grant.','Repayment under the loan’s agreed terms.',['Feature: repayment obligation.'])
q(9,'Name the institution among those studied whose central focus is children’s rights and well-being.','UNICEF.',['Feature: match the children’s mandate.'])
q(10,'Suggest an institution to consult for a fictional food-security project needing agricultural knowledge rather than a general emergency currency loan.','FAO is relevant because of its food and agriculture role. The project still needs suitable local implementation and should not assume an automatic grant.',['Context: agricultural knowledge and food security.','Reason: match mandate to need.'])
